cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SEMEVIA, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "SEMEVIA: fine-grained vehicle recognition with an Identity Evidence Passport"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kumar
    given-names: Aniket
  - family-names: Lakshanaa
    given-names: C
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-11-07"
license: AGPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/DuhItzAniket/SEMEVIA"
abstract: >-
  SEMEVIA detects a vehicle with YOLO11n, identifies its make, model and year among the 196 Stanford Cars
  categories with classical, deep (fine-tuned EfficientNet-B0) and hybrid heads, and reports an Identity
  Evidence Passport: a conformally calibrated candidate set summarised at the most specific level the evidence
  supports, with a six-region Evidence Challenge. Built for the Computer Vision Hackathon 2026 (problem
  statement PS5) by team Hypermetropia. Evaluation results are generated from saved reports (eval_P5_T35.md).
keywords:
  - computer vision
  - fine-grained classification
  - vehicle recognition
  - Stanford Cars
  - object detection
  - conformal prediction
  - uncertainty quantification
  - explainable AI
references:
